# Swill <%= version %>

The Swill framework for a page with no build step.

| File | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `swill.js` | The whole framework |
| `swill-ui.js` | The framework without models, remote data and the richer controls |
| `*.min.js` | The same, minified, without development checks |
| `*.map` | Source maps |
| `resources/swill/` | The framework's themes, images and templates |

Serve these files together, keeping `resources/swill/` beside the
script: the framework finds its resources beside wherever its script was
served from.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <link rel="stylesheet" data-swill-theme href="resources/swill/linear.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main controller="Hello">
    <h1 bind="greeting"></h1>
    <label>Name <input bind="name" autofocus></label>
  </main>
  <script src="swill.js"></script>
  <script>
    class Hello extends Swill.Controller {
      static properties = {name: {default: "world"}};
      get greeting() { return `Hello, ${this.name}!`; }
    }
    Swill.register(Hello);
    Swill.start();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

The same files are served from jsDelivr at this release's tag:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" data-swill-theme href="<%= cdn %>/resources/swill/linear.css">
<script src="<%= cdn %>/swill.js"></script>
```

Getting started: https://github.com/arbales/swill/blob/v<%= version %>/doc/javascript_getting_started.md
